{"source_key":"sha256-db97345053df2686cf66bdd809a5b065","record_index":206,"record_hash":"sha256:ea2d9b310fc46aaa91a23ba39d2fa0460a8eef3840815ece6b720be819fcbc0d","timestamp":"2026-07-23T10:05:07.689Z","kind":"message","source_event_kind":"codex:response_item:message","role":"assistant","text":"The next unit should expose a two-phase prepared checkout operation—not restore the prototype’s standalone preflight helper.\n\nWhy: after a shared ref transaction moves a linked worktree’s symbolic `HEAD`, recomputing checkout state can see the new tree and incorrectly do nothing, leaving its files/index stale. Preparation must retain the old-HEAD calculation across that transaction.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Base the work on the newer sequencing introduced by [PR #14919](https://github.com/gitbutlerapp/gitbutler/pull/14919): prepare → mutate refs → execute checkout.\n\n2. Refactor [function.rs]([REDACTED:path]) into an opaque operation:\n\n   ```rust\n   pub fn prepare_safe_checkout_from_head(\n       new_head_id: gix::ObjectId,\n       repo: &gix::Repository,\n       options: Options,\n   ) -> anyhow::Result<PreparedCheckout<'_>>;\n\n   impl PreparedCheckout<'_> {\n       pub fn execute(self) -> anyhow::Result<Outcome>;\n   }\n   ```\n\n   Preparation performs conflict detection and captures the adjusted destination tree, changed paths, checkout options, and original HEAD state. It must not change the workdir, index, or refs.\n\n3. Preserve every existing caller:\n\n   - `safe_checkout_from_head()` becomes `prepare(...)? .execute()`.\n   - `safe_checkout_from_head_with_pre_checkout()` from PR #14919 becomes prepare → callback → execute.\n   - No caller or signature churn outside `but-core`.\n\n4. Add real linked-worktree coverage in [checkout.rs]([REDACTED:path]):\n\n   - Prepare while refs point to the old commits, move the shared refs, then execute and prove both linked worktrees’ files and private indexes update.\n   - Prove symbolic `HEAD`s remain attached and unrelated dirt survives.\n   - Make the second worktree conflict during preparation and prove neither worktree, index, nor ref was changed.\n\n5. Validate with:\n\n   ```text\n   cargo test -p but-core --test core worktree::checkout\n   cargo check -p but-rebase -p but-workspace --all-targets\n   cargo fmt --all -- --check\n   ```\n\n## Next Editor unit\n\nOnce this lands, [materialization]([REDACTED:path]) can:\n\n1. Persist editor-created objects.\n2. Open every target repository while refs still have their old values.\n3. Prepare all primary and linked-worktree checkouts.\n4. Perform one shared ref transaction.\n5. Execute all prepared checkouts with `skip_head_update: true`.\n6. Refresh the workspace projection.\n\nLinked worktrees should reject conflict-encoded commits; the managed workspace checkout may opt in. Worktree identity should later come from [WorktreeEntry]([REDACTED:path]), not by restoring worktree names to graph traversal tips.\n\nSkipped for this unit: `Editor`, graph, feature-flag, and context changes. Also keep `origin/jt/newcheckout` separate; the opaque operation lets that algorithm change later without disturbing orchestration.\n\nI couldn’t access the private GB-1753 text here, so this plan is grounded in the current tree, the prototype history, and the newer checkout branches. No files were changed.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:1120-1124|note=[prior editor boundary and downstream validation context]\n<[REDACTED:path]>\n<rollout_ids>\n[REDACTED:entropy]\n<[REDACTED:path]>\n<[REDACTED:path]>","tool_name":null,"tool_input":null,"source_record":{"timestamp":"2026-07-23T10:05:07.689Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"[REDACTED:entropy]","role":"assistant","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"[REDACTED:entropy]"},"phase":"final_answer"}}}